<title>USA: Boeing sells three 737-700s to Air Pacific.</title>
<headline>Boeing sells three 737-700s to Air Pacific.</headline>
<dateline>SEATTLE 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boeing said Friday Fiji's Air Pacific is buying three of its next-generation 737-700 aircraft in lieu of an existing commitment to purchase a 767-300ER.</p>
<p>Boeing said the first of the aircraft will be delivered in December.  It said Air Pacific is the first customer in the Pacific to buy the aircraft.</p>
<p>Boeing said the 737-700's will be powered by engines produced by CFM International, a joint venture of General Electric Co and SNECMA of France.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
